---
import './keys.css';
import { encodingExample, tuples } from './encoding.mjs';
const initial = encodingExample('joined');
---
<figure class="key-figure" data-encoding>
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 2</span>Two tuples, one joined string</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="controls"><label for="key-encoding">Encoding</label><select id="key-encoding"><option value="joined">Join with colons</option><option value="json">Fixed JSON array</option></select></div>
  <div class="pair">{tuples.map(([shop,id],i) => <div class="box"><div class="label">Request {i + 1}</div><strong>Shop: <code>{shop}</code></strong><strong>Product: <code>{id}</code></strong><span>↓ stored key</span><code data-key={i}>{initial.keys[i]}</code></div>)}</div>
  <p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite">The joined keys are identical. The separator has lost the boundary between shop and product.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>A deliberate extension allowing colons inside identifiers. Both requests use en-GB and GBP. Switch to a fixed JSON array and the boundaries survive; either tuple can be recovered from its encoding.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Both encodings, as text</summary><p>Joining [“north:outlet”, “P7”] and [“north”, “outlet:P7”] produces the same middle string, north:outlet:P7. JSON arrays preserve each string as its own element, so [“north:outlet”,“P7”,“en-GB”,“GBP”] differs from [“north”,“outlet:P7”,“en-GB”,“GBP”].</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { encodingExample } from './encoding.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-encoding]').forEach(root => {
   const select = root.querySelector('select');
   select?.addEventListener('change', () => {
     const result = encodingExample(select.value);
     root.querySelectorAll('[data-key]').forEach((element,i) => { element.textContent = result.keys[i]; });
     const output = root.querySelector('[data-result]');
     if (output) output.textContent = result.same
       ? 'The joined keys are identical. The separator has lost the boundary between shop and product.'
       : 'The JSON keys differ. Each string keeps its boundary, including any colon inside it.';
   });
 });
</script>
